  clock: 3  # d627
  nonce: d627  # d627
  message: "Fixed in PR #1556 (merge 9f400e64fc), alongside WI-forof. Root cause confirmed: _behaviour_edges matched impls by name only. Fix: Elixir @callback symbols now carry meta['arity'] (the key Erlang -callback symbols use) and _behaviour_edges filters candidates with overload_arity.narrow_by_arity (shared helper; clause arity from meta['parameters'], unknown kept). Evidence: analyze_elixir on the item's repro (@callback f(term) in B; M: @behaviour B, def f(a) line 6, def f(a, b) line 7) on dev -> exactly one edge, dispatches_to B.f -> M.f at line 6. Test: test_elixir_protocols.py::TestBehaviourCallbackArity. Corpus: 10 false callback edges removed on phoenix (Phoenix.Socket.Transport.connect/1 -> UserSocket connect/2,3; those clauses keep their correct Phoenix.Socket.connect dispatch), 0 change on plausible/livebook/nex-framework."  # d627
